define assets as config with
  predict_distance = 1
end

scene start
  The harbour lights come on one by one along the quay, and the water holds every one of them.
  A ferry horn sounds somewhere beyond the breakwater, low and long, and the gulls lift from the rail.
  -> quay
end

scene quay
  Gulls settle again on the rail of the old pier, shuffling and calling as the evening cools.
  The tide turns, and the moored boats swing slowly round on their ropes to face the open sea.
  -> crossing
end

scene crossing
  A lamp is lit in the wheelhouse, and the deckhands coil the last of the ropes by the gangway.
  ((play sound bell))
  The quay bell rings once as the ferry pulls away into open water, its wake spreading pale.
  The wind picks up as the harbour falls behind, and the deck rocks under a long slow swell.
  ((play music voyage))
  Music drifts up from the saloon below, slow and steady, and carries far across the water.
  The lights of the town shrink to a thin bright line along the edge of the dark.
end
